[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539480018","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112865#issuecomment-3539480018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112865","id":3539480018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S-C3S","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T23:34:57Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T23:34:57Z","body":"This is just a numerical precision limitation. You can never compare floating point numbers with exact equality as even the order of operations can yield different results. The absolute differences of get_scale() when being rotated are on the order of 1e-8. If you want to compare floating point numbers for equality you should use `a.is_equal_approx()`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539480018/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539527854","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112865#issuecomment-3539527854","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112865","id":3539527854,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S-Oiu","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T00:23:19Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T00:23:19Z","body":"In saying this the documentation needs to state that rotation does effect scale. Otherwise others will overlook it as being a cause of errors","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539527854/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539549091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112865#issuecomment-3539549091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112865","id":3539549091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S-Tuj","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T00:41:16Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T00:41:16Z","body":"Mathematically it doesn't but any modification of the basis will likely cause strict equality to fail due to the aforementioned floating point limitations. Though this isn't specific to godot but computers in general, mentioning it somewhere for people who are new to programming is probably worthwhile.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539549091/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3540572771","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112865#issuecomment-3540572771","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112865","id":3540572771,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TCNpj","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T08:39:55Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T08:39:55Z","body":"So the main problem is that the documentation states this function is not effected by rotation when it is.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae61f691-b028-47f6-b68d-e09a0af54140)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3540572771/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544944570","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112865#issuecomment-3544944570","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112865","id":3544944570,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TS4-6","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T04:13:12Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T14:03:27Z","body":"As mentioned above https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112865#issuecomment-3539480018, it is mathematically incorrect to say that rotation affects scale, it just the issue of floating-point errors.\n\nFor example:\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar t3d1: Transform3D = Transform3D()\n\tt3d1 = t3d1.scaled_local(Vector3(0.123456, 0.123456, 0.123456))\n\tprint(str(t3d1.basis.get_scale().x) + \", \" + str(t3d1.basis.get_scale().y) + \", \" + str(t3d1.basis.get_scale().z))\n\n\tvar t3d2: Transform3D = Transform3D().rotated(Vector3(1, 1, 1).normalized(), PI * 0.123456)\n\tt3d2 = t3d2.scaled_local(Vector3(0.123456, 0.123456, 0.123456))\n\tprint(str(t3d2.basis.get_scale().x) + \", \" + str(t3d2.basis.get_scale().y) + \", \" + str(t3d2.basis.get_scale().z))\n```\noutput:\n```\n0.12345600128174, 0.12345600128174, 0.12345600128174\n0.12345599383116, 0.12345599383116, 0.12345599383116\n```\n\nSo if documenting this, it should be like \"Scale is stored in and retrieved from a matrix which is constructed by multiplying a normalized rotation matrix by a scale, so rotation's floating-point errors affect scale precision\".","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544944570/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544977097","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112865#issuecomment-3544977097","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112865","id":3544977097,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TTA7J","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T04:30:00Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T04:30:00Z","body":"Something like that would be awesome, it's just to prevent someone from overlooking it because it will always show as not the same once it's rotated.\n\nEven though **theoretical it should not change its value,** in its use any rotation results in the get_scale() no longer returning the same value. Meaning that the returned value of get_scale() will always be effected by rotation due to floating point errors, so it's not correct to say the function is not affected by rotation when it is.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544977097/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3545079602","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112865#issuecomment-3545079602","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112865","id":3545079602,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TTZ8y","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T05:16:42Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T05:16:42Z","body":"I just realized this this would have more implications for people looking to compare the sizes of 2 in games objects via scale\nwhen checking this I noticed you can actually see in the editor when your objects rotation changes the perceived scale, as you get the option to reset scale\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a962f48-b4e7-4931-858f-c7b626f69940","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3545079602/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]